@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+# Telemetry packet, version 2
+
+All numbers are little endian.
+
+| Offset | Size | Field |
+|---|---|---|
+| 0 | 2 | Magic `TL` |
+| 2 | 1 | Version, always 2 |
+| 3 | 4 | Device ID |
+| 7 | 2 | Sample count N, at most 1024 |
+| 9 | 6 N | Samples: 2 bytes sensor ID, 4 bytes signed value |
+| 9 + 6 N | 1 | Label length L, 0 to 31 |
+| 10 + 6 N | L | Label, ASCII, no NUL |
+| 10 + 6 N + L | 2 | CRC-16/CCITT-FALSE of bytes 2 to 9 + 6 N + L |
+
+The collector keeps the label NUL-terminated in a 32-byte field, so a label has at most 31 bytes.
+
+A packet that fails a check is dropped and counted. The device sends the next one after its interval.
